mechanism:
1. Agent (new module wrwl/grow.py, class GrowAgent):
- frozen source trunk up to z, as in CoFork step 1;
- trainable readout R' = clone of L4;
- global log-std reset to -0.5;
- a preallocated pool of M = 64 units u = tanh(A x~ + b), with input x~ = [x / obs_std ; h1] (the normalised state plus the first frozen layer, so new units can see what the deeper impressions discarded), output weights V = 0 and an active mask m.
The mean is R'(z) + V (m * u).

4. Closed-form growth, using TINY's linearised two-SVD solution:
- whiten x~ with W = (Cov x~ + eps I)^(-1/2);
- form S = mean_i W(x~_i - mean) r_i^T (d x 8) and take its SVD, S = P Lambda Q^T;
- null: compute the top singular value after permuting r across whole (env, iteration) blocks, 50 permutations;
- directions whose singular value exceeds the null maximum on 2 consecutive checks are significant;
- add up to 4 units per event: a_j = W^T P[:, j], rescaled to unit pre-activation std on the batch; b_j = -a_j . mean(x~); V[:, j] = 0 (function-preserving);
- zero the Adam moments of the new rows and set m_j = 1.

6. Controls:
- AliasGrow-rand: the same addition schedule as a paired AliasGrow run, with random whitened directions at the same scaling;
- LoRA-matched: rank-r adapters on the frozen L2 and L3 with B = 0 at init, r chosen to match AliasGrow's final trainable-parameter count (about 1024 r);
- frozen-readout: no growth.

pilot.metric:
Stage 0: held-out R^2 of the target expert's actions, and its gain per added unit, by phase. Stages 1-3:
- steps to eval success >= 0.8 (per task for MT; right-censored; median over seeds) and normalised AUC;
- growth logs: units added, residual energy explained, and where the new units' activation variance sits;
- for Stage 1, per-task success curves and per-task gradient cosine in the actor versus the critic (as MTBench measured).

pilot.success:
Stage 0 passes if, on at least one pair, 32 TINY units raise held-out R^2 by at least 0.03 more than 32 random units, and at least 50% of the TINY gain falls in at most 30% of the states.
Stage 2 passes if, on T90 or T180:
- AliasGrow's median steps-to-80% is at most 0.8 x min(frozen-readout, LoRA-matched, AliasGrow-rand);
- it is no slower than min(scratch, ft-reset);
- every AliasGrow seed is faster than every AliasGrow-rand seed.
Stage 1 licenses Stage 3 only if all three hold:
- joint MT-PPO needs more than 1.5x the summed single-task steps to bring all four directions to 0.8;
- separate actors close at least 50% of that gap;
- per-task critic heads close less than 50% of it.
Stage 3 passes if MT-AliasGrow beats both random task-gated growth and the 2x-width actor by at least 1.25x at matched parameters.

pilot.kill:
Stop before any RL if Stage 0 fails on every pair: targeted directions do not beat random ones even with oracle targets.
Kill AliasGrow if any of these holds:
- it is within 15% of AliasGrow-rand on both T90 and T180;
- the growth test fires in fewer than 2 of 6 runs (no bottleneck is detectable from the RL signal);
- ft-reset is at least as fast on both, which would mean M1's negative transfer came from the transferred critic and the small std, not from aliasing.
Kill the multi-task extension if joint MT-PPO is within 1.25x the summed single-task steps, or if per-task critic heads close most of the gap (critic-side conflict, as MTBench found).

